//@version=6
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  SKULD — one indicator, self-switching by chart timeframe.
//  Primary chart of record: 30-minute (2026-08-07 — levels give the entry
//  precision; the bar TF gives the signal QUALITY. Everything bar-based
//  scales with the chart: reaction window, validity, cooldown, velocity).
//
//  v2.9.2 (2026-08-10): BRT GROWS UP — a wick through VWAP is not a
//     break-retest. Break now requires ACCEPTANCE (inAcc consecutive closes
//     beyond the escape margin, IB's standard, signed counter per cluster);
//     the retest requires SEPARATION (min bars after the accepted break),
//     DEPTH (low reaches within half a cluster width of the level),
//     REJECTION (MR's close-position standard on the retest bar) and an
//     EffScore ≥ the regime trade floor from the approach side. Chop that
//     pokes one close through and dips a wick no longer fires.
//  v2.9.1 (2026-08-10): SIGNAL LIFECYCLE — a ticket is a resting limit,
//     track it like one. Fill (price returns to E) must happen before SL/TP
//     count — unfilled tickets can no longer stamp "TP ✓". Price tags T1
//     without filling = "RAN — unfilled" dim stamp, ticket AND HUD signal
//     clear instantly (WAITING shows the next levels instead of a stale
//     BUY block screaming over a finished move). Session-gap exit also
//     clears the HUD.
//  v2.9.0 (2026-08-07): CONSISTENCY — the last fixed ticks die · TWAP.
//   · Outcome stamps print the TICKET'S OWN distances (planE/T1/S ticks),
//     not the legacy 32/48 — no more "TP ✓ +32t" under a taller T1 line.
//   · APP is ADVISORY now: dim label + one-shot per level, no ticket, no
//     count, no alert. It was the last play still emitting fixed-tick
//     E/S/T. A chase has no structure behind the entry — it gets a read.
//   · Session TWAP: time-weighted average since session open — dim line
//     beside VWAP + rank-6 pool level (toggle). VWAP+TWAP agreeing = one
//     strong magnet; split wide = volume arrived away from time-average.
//   · TUNE debug row shows regime truth (dATR · width · tier) instead of
//     the legacy tick pair; the tick inputs are relabeled LEGACY seeds.
//  v2.8.0 (2026-08-07): BRT JOINS THE VOICE · HUD REBUILT TO THE DECK SPEC.
//   · BRT (break-retest) ON by default and fires through dynamic
//     construction: retest of a punched cluster holds → entry at the
//     cluster edge, structure stop, TP1 in front of the next qualifying
//     level, room gate. Room fails → NOTRADE, cluster state stays armed so
//     a later retest inside the watch window retries. Six alertconditions:
//     BUY/SELL MR · IB · BRT, one pipe format.
//   · HUD rebuilt (the teaching-deck mockups won): header row "SKULD ·
//     SYMBOL TF | WAITING/SIGNAL/STRUCTURE", aligned columns (side+name ·
//     price · ±dist · score), ▲ short zone purple · ▼ long zone green,
//     gold scores, ROOM row shows the available ticks per side (L OK·34t),
//     SIGNAL grid labels E/S/T1/R individually colored (S red · T1 green ·
//     R cyan), VALID shown as a clock (mm:ss). Table rebuilt on the last
//     bar — no stale cells between states.
//  v2.7.0 (2026-08-07): IB JOINS THE VOICE · REACT DE-SPAM · BRIGHTER SIGNAL.
//   · IB play fires through the SAME dynamic construction as MR: entry =
//     broken IB edge (retest resting limit), structure stop inside the
//     balance, TP1 in front of the next opposing qualifying level, room
//     gate included ("see money, take money" on breakouts too). Room fails
//     → NOTRADE event and the per-side shot is NOT consumed — a later
//     re-acceptance retries with fresh room. Four alertconditions now:
//     BUY/SELL MR + BUY/SELL IB, same pipe format. Two-play coverage:
//     MR eats balance days, IB eats trend days.
//   · REACT labels print only at/above a score threshold (input, default
//     75 — the defended touches). Every score still computes and feeds
//     stats, gates and the feed; the chart just stops wallpapering 0% ✗.
//   · APPR chart labels: DRIVE (freight train) only by default — GRIND /
//     DRIFT stay in the HUD/feed (toggle restores 2.6 behavior).
//   · Signal brightness: chart fire label fully opaque; HUD SIGNAL block
//     fill stronger, E/S/T1/R row larger.
//  v2.6.0 (2026-08-07): DYNAMIC TARGETING — every level carries a live,
//     directional, regime-aware EFFECTIVE SCORE; the only outputs are the
//     few levels in play and a limit-order-ready MR signal with a dynamic
//     TP1 at the next working level ("see money, take money").
//   · EFFECTIVE SCORE engine: per-atomic-level reaction memory, keyed by
//     stable identity (names; HVN/LVN by price bucket), per approach
//     direction (fromBelow |B · fromAbove |A). Touch outcomes (HOLD/BREAK,
//     resolved over a 3-bar window) feed an EWMA hold rate; score =
//     baseRank × clamp(0.5 + holdRate, 0.5, 1.5) × 0.85^touchesToday.
//     A low-rank level broken 3+ times decays below thresholds and leaves
//     the chart — breaking finally has a consequence.
//   · REGIME engine: daily ATR(14) percentile (60-day window) + VIX bump
//     → LOW/NORM/HIGH/EXTREME tier. Tier sets cluster width (×dATR),
//     display/trade score floors, TP floor/cap and stop buffer. Width
//     recomputes only at session boundaries or tier change (no identity
//     churn). All cut points and table values are inputs.
//   · DYNAMIC TRADE CONSTRUCTION (MR): entry = cluster edge offset into
//     the zone (resting-limit workflow) · stop = far edge + buffer×dATR ·
//     TP1 = front edge of the FIRST opposing qualifying cluster minus a
//     standoff — never through a working level. Room gate: tpDist ≥
//     max(minR × stopDist, tpFloor × dATR) or NO TRADE (never skip to the
//     next cluster). Open field → TP1 = entry ± tpCap × dATR. R emitted.
//   · MR SIGNAL GATES: EffScore ≥ minTradeScore · room gate · initiative
//     standdown (approach velocity + consecutive closes) · lower-TF delta
//     standdown (one-sided flow into the level = absorption absent).
//   · EXECUTION display: only the nearest K qualifying clusters per side
//     (EffScore ≥ minDisplayScore), labels carry score + directional
//     record (3H/1B). STRUCTURE mode keeps the full map. Imbalance boxes
//     hidden by default (real footprint lives on another chart).
//   · HUD: trade-entry info only — nearest qualifying level each side +
//     ROOM check while waiting; E/S/T1/R + validity countdown on signal.
//     The old 13-row system panel moved behind showDebugHud.
//   · ALERTS (2.6; 2.7 adds IB): pipe-delimited with E/S/TP1/R/level/
//     score, readable off a phone.
//     APP/BRT plays still detect and draw, but no longer alert. The
//     ledger feed events are opt-in now (feedAlerts default OFF); NOTRADE
//     events report room-gate kills.
//  v2.5.2 (2026-08-06): label offset default 1 bar — level labels hug the
//     current candle instead of floating off-screen right.
//  v2.5 (2026-08-06): ALL SESSIONS — Asia · London · NY are first-class.
//   · Per-session VWAP + σ bands: reset at each session open, live in every
//     session (the extension-zone reference finally exists off-NY).
//   · Per-session Initial Balance: the first N minutes (input, 60) of
//     WHICHEVER session just opened. IB play, IB row and the day-type IB
//     component now work in all three sessions.
//   · Signal pools use the LIVE session's H/L (sesH/sesL, rank 8) instead of
//     the NY-only day extremes.
//   · Sessions-only signal window (default ON, per the trader's ask): the
//     16:00-18:00 ET settlement gap pauses signals; Asia open resumes them.
//   · The trading day starts at the Asia open (18:00 ET): signal counter
//     and plan drawings reset there, not at the NY open.
//   · Session naming stays ASIA everywhere (his call).
//     and level-name history key off them).
//  v2.4.2 (2026-07-30): REACT prints as a percent ("REACT 11% ✗") on the
//     label and the row — the score is the share of possible defense
//     evidence at the touch. The feed keeps the raw number (score=11).
//  v2.4.1 (2026-07-30): STAMP renamed REACT everywhere user-facing — the
//     number is a 0-100 reaction-quality score (share of possible defense
//     evidence), NOT a touch count; the old word read like one. Touch
//     counts stay separate (·T2 on NEAREST). Feed event is EVT=REACT.
//  v2.4 (2026-07-30): DAY TYPE · APPROACH GRADE · TOUCH REACT · LEDGER FEED.
//   All three features are ADVISORY/DISPLAY-ONLY at defaults — with every new
//   toggle at its default the script's signals, levels, rows and drawings
//   behave exactly as v2.3 (the new rows and feed alerts are the only
//   additions). Enforcement is opt-in.
//   · DAY TYPE row: BALANCE / TREND▲ / TREND▼ / TRANSITION per session.
//     Components: open vs prior value, IB extension hold, value migration,
//     15m one-timeframing, cumulative session delta trend — summed to a
//     score T with a participation gate (session range vs ADR(10)) and
//     2-evaluation hysteresis. Optional play matrix (OFF / ADVISORY /
//     ENFORCE): reversal-at-level benched against strong trend, break-retest
//     benched in balance; benched signals stay counted via the feed.
//   · APPR row (execution only): how price is ARRIVING at the next ranked
//     cluster — DRIVE (fast, directional, shallow pullbacks), GRIND
//     (rotational two-way), DRIFT (thin, low participation) from path
//     efficiency, speed vs ATR, max pullback and delta alignment over the
//     approach window. Playbook hint lives in the tooltip, logic untouched.
//   · TOUCH STAMP (execution only): at a ranked-cluster touch, score the
//     evidence 0-100 the same way every time — delta flip vs the approach
//     (30), where the touch bar's volume sat in its range (25, an
//     APPROXIMATION of footprint order flow from lower-TF volume — Pine
//     cannot read true bid/ask), rejection structure on the close (25),
//     effort/result divergence (20). ✓ ≥70 · – 40-69 · ✗ <40, printed at
//     the touch and in the STAMP row. Optional MR gate ships OFF.
//   · LEDGER FEED: pipe-delimited alert() events (TOUCH / STAMP / DAYTYPE /
//     APPR / BENCHED) + per-level daily touch counter — the journal's data
//     feed. Request budget unchanged: still ONE lower-TF call (tuple now
//     carries hl2 for the stamp bins).
//  v2.3 (2026-07-30): CLOCK + ZONE FRESHNESS — tournament-ledger-driven.
//   · CLOCK row + cold-hour tag: prime hours (default 0800-1030 ET) vs cold
//     hours (default 0000-0100, 0700-0800, 1100-1200, 1500-1600 ET — the
//     ledger's proven bleed windows) on the dashboard; alerts fired in cold
//     hours carry a "COLD HOUR" tag. Info only, session inputs, retune as
//     the data moves. Nothing is ever blocked.
//   · Zone freshness decay: every pass through a zone consumes the resting
//     orders that made it. Zones now count touches — first touch DIMS the
//     box (the trade was that touch), N touches (default 2) retires it.
//     Close-through the far side still kills instantly. Fresh + untouched =
//     trustworthy; chopped-through repeatedly = gone, not wallpaper.
//  v2.2.1 (2026-07-30): zone tune after first live day — zone = origin
//     THIRD of the impulse body (not the whole body; trend days painted the
//     chart solid), duplicate same-side overlapping zones suppressed,
//     defaults tightened (share 0.80, vol 1.2x, max 4/side).
//  v2.2 (2026-07-30): READABILITY + IMBALANCE ZONES.
//   · Right-edge fit: label offset default 3 bars (was 8) — lines/labels sit
//     next to price on every chart style, footprint included.
//   · Dashboard: position selectable (any corner) + brand palette (dark card,
//     colored state text — no more stock green/red fills).
//   · Signals: ONE clean label per fire (play + direction + score), brand
//     colors, size selectable. Triangles/plotshapes and the long plan text
//     label are gone. Plan lines (E/S/T) + outcome stamps stay. Stop line is
//     red now; purple stays the short-direction brand color.
//   · IMBALANCE ZONES (footprint proxy): per-bar buy/sell volume split from
//     the lower-TF feed already powering the profiles. A bar whose one-sided
//     volume share ≥ ratio (default 75%) on real volume prints a zone box
//     (bar body, extended right) — the Pine approximation of stacked
//     footprint imbalances. Zones die when price closes through the far
//     side. Clusters sitting inside a live zone get +2 rank (input) and a ◆
//     tag — level + resting imbalance = the confluence you trade toward.
//     NOTE: Pine cannot read the chart's own footprint boxes — this proxy is
//     computed from lower-TF up/down volume instead.
//
//  v2.1 (2026-07-21): APP toward-play — ride INTO a powerful level once
//     inside the approach window (1.0-1.5x target). With-move close, level
//     untouched in the lookback, one shot per level. Target lands at/just in
//     front of the level — never hold through it.
//  v2 (2026-07-21): DEVELOPING LEVELS ENGINE + VP visual overhaul.
//   · Live developing levels are first-class ranked levels now:
//       sPOC  (developing session POC)  rank 6 (session 1 + POC 5)
//       sVAH/sVAL (developing session VA) rank 4 (session 1 + VA 3)
//       dPOC  (developing DAY POC)        rank 8 (day 3 + POC 5)
//       dVAH/dVAL (developing day VA)     rank 6 (day 3 + VA 3)
//     Recomputed on every confirmed close from the fine-bin profiles,
//     drawn + ★-labeled, included in the MR pool and NEAREST panel.
//     The chart finally reacts to the CURRENT session, not just priors.
//   · VP style input: "Lines" (default — clean, draw your own profiles),
//     "Bars" (right-edge anchored, borderless thin rows), "Off".
//   · Defaults follow the 2026-07-21 shipped tuning: wick 0.55, cooldown 5,
//     tol 2×W, lunch/RTH-only/hard-cap gates OFF (all are toggles — flip for
//     strict plan mode). Dev-level signals test the LAST CONFIRMED level
//     snapshot; dev lines refresh on the first confirmed close after a
//     session roll (one live bar of lag at the boundary is by design).
//
//  ≥ switch TF (default 1H)  → STRUCTURE mode: weekly + daily ranked level
//     map, composite profile, clusters. No signals — this is the map.
//  < switch TF               → EXECUTION mode: session VWAP ±1σ/±2σ, ranked
//     level clusters, developing levels, and the plays:
//       IB  — THE set play: initial-balance acceptance break (9:30–10:30 ET)
//       MR  — everything else: reaction wick at a high-rank cluster
//       BRT — punched level retested from the other side and held
//       APP — approach: ride into a powerful level inside the window
//
//  LEVEL RANKING:  rank = scope + kind.
//     scope: session 1 · day 3 · week 5
//     kind:  POC 5 · VAH/VAL 3 · H/L 3 · HVN 2 · LVN 1
//     dynamic (fixed): VWAP 10 · day H/L 8 · dPOC 8 · ±2σ 6 · ONH/ONL 6 ·
//                      sPOC 6 · dVAH/dVAL 6 · IB 4 · sVAH/sVAL 4
//  CLUSTERING: levels within cluster width merge; rank = SUM; price =
//     rank-weighted mean. stars: ≥10 ★★★★★ · 8–9 ★★★★ · 6–7 ★★★ · 4–5 ★★ · ★
//
//  Candle-close confirmed only. No lookahead. No repaint.
//  One alert covers all: "Any alert() function call".
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
indicator("SKULD 2.9 — Dynamic Targeting · MR + IB + BRT", "SKULD", overlay = true, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500)

// ── ASSET AUTO-TUNE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool isES = syminfo.root == "ES" or syminfo.root == "MES"

// ── INPUTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
const string TZ = "America/New_York"
const string GM = "Mode & trade math"
const string GS = "Sessions (ET)"
const string GP = "Profile engine"
const string GK = "Level ranking & clusters"
const string GV = "Session volume profile"
const string GE = "Developing levels (live)"
const string GW = "VWAP & dynamic levels"
const string GI = "Play · IB (the set play)"
const string GR = "Play · MR (reaction at level)"
const string GB = "Play · BRT (break-retest continuation)"
const string GA = "Play · APP (toward a powerful level)"
const string GT = "Discipline & trade plan"
const string GZ = "Imbalance zones (footprint proxy)"
const string GY = "Day Type"
const string GAPR = "Approach"
const string GSTP = "Touch React (0-100)"
const string GLF = "Ledger Feed"
const string GD = "Dashboard"
const string GC = "Colors & lines"
const string GES = "Effective Score"
const string GRG = "Regime (ATR + VIX)"
const string GTC = "Trade Construction"
const string GSG = "Signal Gates"

string inModeTf = input.timeframe("60", "Structure mode at/above TF", group = GM, tooltip = "Chart TF >= this = STRUCTURE map (no signals). Below = EXECUTION mode.")
int inTgtT  = input.int(0, "LEGACY width seed ticks (0 = auto: 32 NQ / 8 ES)", minval = 0, group = GM, tooltip = "NOT a trade target since 2.6 — every ticket's E/S/T1 is built dynamically from the regime engine (dATR tier). This only seeds cluster width before the first daily ATR arrives and sizes the APP advisory window.")
int inStopT = input.int(0, "LEGACY stop seed ticks (0 = auto: 48 NQ / 12 ES)", minval = 0, group = GM, tooltip = "NOT a trade stop since 2.6 — stops are structure + regime buffer. Kept only for the MR touch-band fallback geometry.")

string rthSess   = input.session("0930-1600", "NY session (ET)", group = GS)
int    inIbMin   = input.int(60, "Initial balance: minutes from EACH session open", minval = 15, maxval = 120, group = GS, tooltip = "Every session (Asia, London, NY) builds its own IB over its first N minutes. IB play, IB row and the day-type IB read follow the active session.")
string onSess    = input.session("1800-0930", "Overnight (ONH/ONL)", group = GS)
string sAsia     = input.session("1800-0300", "Asia session (ET)", group = GS)
string sLdn      = input.session("0300-0930", "London session (ET)", group = GS)

int    inRows  = input.int(24, "Extraction rows per profile", minval = 6, maxval = 60, group = GP)
float  inVA    = input.float(70, "Value area %", minval = 50, maxval = 95, group = GP)
float  inHvnK  = input.float(1.5, "HVN ≥ × avg row volume", step = 0.1, group = GP)
float  inLvnK  = input.float(0.5, "LVN ≤ × avg row volume", step = 0.1, group = GP)
int    inMaxHV = input.int(1, "Max HVN per profile", minval = 0, maxval = 3, group = GP)
int    inMaxLV = input.int(1, "Max LVN per profile", minval = 0, maxval = 3, group = GP)
float  inBin   = input.float(0.0, "Fine bin pts (0 = auto: 1.0 NQ / 0.25 ES)", minval = 0, group = GP)
string inLtf   = input.timeframe("", "Intrabar TF (blank = auto)", group = GP)

float inClW     = input.float(0.0, "Cluster width pts (0 = auto: 25% of target)", minval = 0, group = GK)
int   inMinRank = input.int(6, "Min rank to trade a level", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = GK, tooltip = "MR/BRT fire only on clusters/levels at or above this rank. 6 = ★★★ up. 8 = ★★★★ up. 10 = ★★★★★ only.")
bool  showLvls  = input.bool(true, "Draw cluster lines + labels", group = GK)
int   inMaxL    = input.int(12, "Max clusters shown (nearest kept)", minval = 2, maxval = 40, group = GK)
float inHide    = input.float(0, "Hide clusters farther than (pts, 0 = off)", minval = 0, group = GK)
int   inOff     = input.int(1, "Label offset (bars right)", minval = 1, maxval = 50, group = GK, tooltip = "Bars between the last candle and the line end / label. 1 = hugging price. Bar-based, so it stays put at every zoom and every chart style, footprint included.")
bool  showPx    = input.bool(true, "Show price in labels", group = GK)

string inVpStyle  = input.string("Lines", "Profile style", options = ["Lines", "Bars", "Off"], group = GV, tooltip = "Lines = no histogram, developing levels only (draw profiles by hand). Bars = borderless histogram. Off = nothing.")
string inVpAnchor = input.string("Right edge", "Bars anchor", options = ["Right edge", "Session start"], group = GV)
string inVpSrc    = input.string("Auto", "Profile source", options = ["Auto", "Session", "Day", "Week"], group = GV, tooltip = "Auto = active session in execution mode, developing week in structure mode.")
int    inVpRows   = input.int(30, "Histogram rows", minval = 10, maxval = 60, group = GV)
int    inVpWide   = input.int(14, "Histogram max width (bars)", minval = 5, maxval = 100, group = GV)

bool showDevS   = input.bool(true, "Developing session POC/VAH/VAL (sPOC ★★★ · sVA ★★)", group = GE)
bool showDevD   = input.bool(true, "Developing day POC/VAH/VAL (dPOC ★★★★ · dVA ★★★)", group = GE)
bool inclDevMR  = input.bool(true, "Developing levels fire MR", group = GE, tooltip = "sPOC rank 6, sVAH/sVAL 4, dPOC 8, dVAH/dVAL 6 — gated by min rank like everything else.")

bool showVwap = input.bool(true, "Session VWAP + ±1σ", group = GW)
bool showSd2  = input.bool(true, "±2σ band", group = GW)
bool showOn   = input.bool(true, "ONH/ONL lines", group = GW)
bool inclTwap = input.bool(true, "Session TWAP — line + level (rank 6)", group = GW, tooltip = "Time-weighted average price since session open (execution-desk reference). Drawn dimmer than VWAP; joins the level pool at rank 6. VWAP + TWAP agreeing = one strong magnet; far apart = volume came in away from time-average, trend tell.")

bool enIB     = input.bool(true, "Enable IB play", group = GI)
int  inAcc    = input.int(2, "Acceptance closes beyond IB", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = GI)
int  inMaxBrk = input.int(1, "Max IB signals per side per day", minval = 1, maxval = 3, group = GI)

bool  enMR     = input.bool(true, "Enable MR play", group = GR)
float inWick   = input.float(0.55, "Rejection: close position ≥ (0.5–1)", minval = 0.5, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = GR, tooltip = "Long: close must sit in top fraction of bar range. Short mirrored.")
float inMrTol  = input.float(0.0, "Touch tolerance pts (0 = auto: 2× cluster width — 4 NQ / 1 ES)", minval = 0, group = GR)
bool  useVolMR = input.bool(false, "Require volume ≥ × avg (footprint proxy)", group = GR)
float volKMR   = input.float(1.2, "Volume multiple", step = 0.1, group = GR)
bool  inclVwap = input.bool(true, "Include VWAP (rank 10)", group = GR)
bool  inclSd2  = input.bool(true, "Include ±2σ (rank 6)", group = GR)
bool  inclDay  = input.bool(true, "Include live session H/L (rank 8)", group = GR)
bool  inclON   = input.bool(true, "Include ONH/ONL (rank 6)", group = GR)

bool  enBRT     = input.bool(true, "Enable BRT play (break-retest)", group = GB, tooltip = "ON since 2.8 — broken level retested from the other side and held. Fires through the same dynamic construction and alerts as MR/IB. Trend-day continuation entries AT structure.")
float inBrtEsc  = input.float(0.0, "Break margin pts (0 = auto: cluster width)", minval = 0, group = GB)
int   inBrtWatch = input.int(20, "Retest watch window (bars)", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = GB)
int   brtMinGap  = input.int(3, "Retest: min bars after break", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = GB, tooltip = "The retest cannot fire until this many bars after the break is ACCEPTED — separation is what makes it a retest instead of the same chop that faked the break.")

bool  enAPP        = input.bool(true, "APP advisory (ride toward a wall)", group = GA, tooltip = "ADVISORY since 2.9 — dim label when a with-move ride into a powerful level sets up. No ticket, no alert, no count: a chase has no structure behind the entry, so it gets a read, not numbers. The reaction AT the level is the next decision (usually an MR or BRT).")
int   inAppRank    = input.int(8, "Min rank of destination level", minval = 4, maxval = 30, group = GA)
float inAppNear    = input.float(1.0, "Window near edge (× target)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.1, group = GA, tooltip = "Level must be at least this many target-distances away, so the fixed target lands in FRONT of the level.")
float inAppFar     = input.float(1.5, "Window far edge (× target)", minval = 0.6, step = 0.1, group = GA)
float inAppPos     = input.float(0.55, "With-move close position ≥", minval = 0.5, maxval = 1, step = 0.05, group = GA)
int   inAppNoTouch = input.int(10, "Level untouched for (bars)", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = GA, tooltip = "No wick within tolerance of the level in this lookback — do not chase into a level that just rejected.")
bool  inAppDyn     = input.bool(true, "Include dynamic levels (VWAP · day H/L · dPOC · ±2σ · ON)", group = GA)

int  inMaxSig = input.int(3, "Max signals per day (3-trade rule)", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = GT)
bool inHardCap = input.bool(false, "Hard-stop signals at max", group = GT, tooltip = "ON = indicator stops firing after max (plan: 'indicator stops signaling after 3 fires'). OFF = counter keeps counting, signals keep coming — display-only discipline.")
bool inRthOnly = input.bool(false, "Signals only in NY RTH", group = GT, tooltip = "OFF = signals also fire in Asia and London.")
bool inSessOnly = input.bool(true, "Signals only during sessions (pause 16:00-18:00 ET)", group = GT, tooltip = "Asia, London and NY each start and stop the engine at their open and close. The settlement gap between the NY close and the Asia open fires nothing.")
int  inCd     = input.int(5, "Cooldown bars between signals", minval = 0, group = GT)
bool useLunch = input.bool(false, "Lunch blackout", group = GT)
string lunchSess = input.session("1130-1330", "Lunch window (ET)", group = GT)
